{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/dao/space/dht.cljc | sed -n '1152,1228p'; nl -ba src/cljc/dao/space/dht.cljc | sed -n '1260,1308p'; rg -n 'fetch|deadline|exhausted' src/cljc/dao/jing/dht/client.cljc | head -45; nl -ba src/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc | sed -n '24,83p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/dht.cljc | sed -n '153,160p'; nl -ba docs/design/dao.jing.dht.md | sed -n '1,63p'; rg -n 'forget.*loading|loading.*forget' test/dao/space/dht_test.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"  1152\t(defn load\n  1153\t  \"Start loading `address` with `{:kind k :walk f}`: `f` is `(fn [handle]\n  1154\t   outcome)` over the node's local store, answering\n  1155\t   `{:dao.space.dht/walk :missing :address a}`, `{... :complete :value v}`\n  1156\t   or `{... :invalid :address a-or-nil :defect {:code c ...}}`.  `step`\n  1157\t   fetches each missing address and walks again, and reports `:loaded`\n  1158\t   or `:load-failed` once.  A load already started, loaded or failed is\n  1159\t   left as it is.  Answers the node.\"\n  1160\t  [node address {:keys [kind walk]}]\n  1161\t  (when-not (jing/segment-address? address)\n  1162\t    (throw (ex-info \"dao.space.dht/load takes a segment address\"\n  1163\t                    {:address address})))\n  1164\t  (when-not (ifn? walk)\n  1165\t    (throw (ex-info \"dao.space.dht/load takes a :walk function\" {:kind kind})))\n  1166\t  (if (contains? (:loads node) address)\n  1167\t    node\n  1168\t    (assoc-in node [:loads address]\n  1169\t              {:status :loading :kind kind :walk walk :fetching nil :fetched\n  1170\t               0})))\n  1171\t\n  1172\t\n  1173\t(def index-kind\n  1174\t  \"The `:kind` of a covered-index load.\"\n  1175\t  ::index)\n  1176\t\n  1177\t\n  1178\t(defn load-index\n  1179\t  \"`load` of the published index `manifest-address` names, with the\n  1180\t   covered-index walk: its `:loaded` value is the index's EAVT datoms.\"\n  1181\t  [node manifest-address]\n  1182\t  (when-not (jing/segment-address? manifest-address)\n  1183\t    (throw (ex-info \"dao.space.dht/load-index takes a manifest address\"\n  1184\t                    {:manifest manifest-address})))\n  1185\t  (load node manifest-address {:kind index-kind\n  1186\t                               :walk (index-walk manifest-address)}))\n  1187\t\n  1188\t\n  1189\t(defn load-status\n  1190\t  \"`address`'s load, or nil when none was started:\n  1191\t   `{:status :loading :kind k :fetched n :fetching address-or-nil}`,\n  1192\t   `{:status :loaded :kind k :fetched n :value v}` or\n  1193\t   `{:status :failed :kind k :fetched n :reason reason}`.\"\n  1194\t  [node address]\n  1195\t  (when-let [{:keys [status kind fetched fetching value reason]}\n  1196\t             (get-in node [:loads address])]\n  1197\t    (case status\n  1198\t      :loading {:status status :kind kind :fetched fetched\n  1199\t                :fetching (:address fetching)}\n  1200\t      :loaded {:status status :kind kind :fetched fetched :value value}\n  1201\t      :failed {:status status :kind kind :fetched fetched :reason reason})))\n  1202\t\n  1203\t\n  1204\t(defn forget\n  1205\t  \"`node` without `address`'s terminal load record, so a new `load`\n  1206\t   starts over.  Refused (`:dao.space.dht/loading`) while it loads.\"\n  1207\t  [node address]\n  1208\t  (when (= :loading (get-in node [:loads address :status]))\n  1209\t    (throw (refused ::loading (str address \" is still loading\")\n  1210\t                    {:address address})))\n  1211\t  (update node :loads dissoc address))\n  1212\t\n  1213\t\n  1214\t(defn loaded-datoms\n  1215\t  \"The EAVT datoms of a loaded index, or nil.\"\n  1216\t  [node manifest-address]\n  1217\t  (let [record (get-in node [:loads manifest-address])]\n  1218\t    (when (and (= :loaded (:status record)) (= index-kind (:kind record)))\n  1219\t      (:value record))))\n  1220\t\n  1221\t\n  1222\t(defn loaded-indexes\n  1223\t  \"The covered-index manifests whose load is `:loaded` on `node`, as a\n  1224\t   vector sorted by address text: a load of another kind, one still\n  1225\t   loading and a failed one are not listed.\"\n  1226\t  [node]\n  1227\t  (vec (sort-by str (filter #(loaded-datoms node %) (keys (:loads node))))))\n  1228\t\n  1260\t\n  1261\t(defn- advance-load\n  1262\t  [node m done-by-id]\n  1263\t  (let [{:keys [fetching kind walk], :as record} (get-in node [:loads m])\n  1264\t        done (when fetching (get done-by-id (:id fetching)))]\n  1265\t    (cond\n  1266\t      (and fetching (nil? done)) [node []]\n  1267\t\n  1268\t      ;; the miss cause stays: another load may wait on the same address;\n  1269\t      ;; advance-loads drops it once none does\n  1270\t      (and done (not (:found? done)))\n  1271\t      (let [a (:address fetching)]\n  1272\t        (fail-load node m {::failure :miss :address a\n  1273\t                           :cause (get-in node [:misses a] ::dht/gap)}))\n  1274\t\n  1275\t      :else\n  1276\t      (let [fetched (cond-> (:fetched record) done inc)\n  1277\t            node (update-in node [:loads m] assoc :fetching nil :fetched\n  1278\t                            fetched)\n  1279\t            walked (walk-outcome walk (local node))]\n  1280\t        (case (::walk walked)\n  1281\t          :complete\n  1282\t          [(update-in node [:loads m] #(-> % (assoc :status :loaded :value\n  1283\t                                                    (:value walked))\n  1284\t                                           (dissoc :walk)))\n  1285\t           [(cond-> {::event :loaded :manifest m :kind kind :fetched fetched}\n  1286\t              (= index-kind kind) (assoc :datoms (count (:value walked))))]]\n  1287\t\n  1288\t          :invalid\n  1289\t          (fail-load node m {::failure :invalid :address (:address walked)\n  1290\t                             :defect (:defect walked)})\n  1291\t\n  1292\t          :missing\n  1293\t          (let [a (:address walked)\n  1294\t                {:keys [outcome id], :as asked} (content.step/request-get\n  1295\t                                                  (:client node) a)]\n  1296\t            (case outcome\n  1297\t              (:requested :pending-request)\n  1298\t              [(-> node\n  1299\t                   (assoc :client (:state asked))\n  1300\t                   (assoc-in [:loads m :fetching] {:id id :address a}))\n  1301\t               []]\n  1302\t\n  1303\t              ;; the client still owes a request: ask again next step\n  1304\t              :busy [(assoc node :client (:state asked)) []]\n  1305\t\n  1306\t              (fail-load (assoc node :client (:state asked)) m\n  1307\t                         {::failure :unaskable :address a :outcome\n  1308\t                          outcome}))))))))\nrg: src/cljc/dao/jing/dht/client.cljc: IO error for operation on src/cljc/dao/jing/dht/client.cljc: No such file or directory (os error 2)\n    24\t\n    25\t\n    26\t;; =============================================================================\n    27\t;; Wire shapes (2.1)\n    28\t;; =============================================================================\n    29\t\n    30\t(def ^:private wire-ops\n    31\t  \"The four wire operations. close! never crosses -- the mirror holds\n    32\t   nothing per remote party to close and the owner's close is never\n    33\t   remote -- and attach! never crosses, because it consumes a\n    34\t   descriptor and produces a local handle.\"\n    35\t  #{:dao.stream/descriptor :dao.stream/cursor :dao.stream/next\n    36\t    :dao.stream/append!})\n    37\t\n    38\t\n    39\t(def ^:private protocol-errors\n    40\t  \"The three protocol errors, one answer shape for every operation,\n    41\t   a key instead of an outcome map because no operation's outcome set\n    42\t   can carry them.\"\n    43\t  #{:dao.stream.remote/not-found\n    44\t    :dao.stream.remote/no-surface\n    45\t    :dao.stream.remote/oversize})\n    46\t\n    47\t\n    48\t(defn- well-formed-request?\n    49\t  \"True when `v` is a well-formed request: a map naming its identity\n    50\t   and one of the four wire ops, carrying an args vector and the\n    51\t   asker-minted id. Anything else is dropped as malformed wire input.\"\n    52\t  [v]\n    53\t  (and (map? v)\n    54\t       (contains? v :dao.stream/identity)\n    55\t       (contains? wire-ops (:dao.stream.remote/op v))\n    56\t       (vector? (:dao.stream.remote/args v))\n    57\t       (contains? v :dao.stream.remote/id)))\n    58\t\n    59\t\n    60\t(defn- well-formed-answer?\n    61\t  \"True when `v` is a well-formed answer: a map carrying the id and\n    62\t   the identity and either a protocol error or an outcome map.\"\n    63\t  [v]\n    64\t  (and (map? v)\n    65\t       (contains? v :dao.stream.remote/id)\n    66\t       (contains? v :dao.stream/identity)\n    67\t       (or (contains? protocol-errors (:dao.stream.remote/error v))\n    68\t           (stream/outcome-map? v))))\n    69\t\n    70\t\n    71\t(defn- required-surface\n    72\t  \"The declared surface `op` needs, under the fixed mapping: cursor\n    73\t   and next need :reader, append! needs :writer, descriptor needs no\n    74\t   surface and is always answerable.\"\n    75\t  [op]\n    76\t  (case op\n    77\t    (:dao.stream/cursor :dao.stream/next) :reader\n    78\t    :dao.stream/append! :writer\n    79\t    nil))\n    80\t\n    81\t\n    82\t(defn- error-answer\n    83\t  \"The protocol-error answer shape, with the id and identity the\n   153\t(defn snapshots\n   154\t  \"The node's snapshot set (7.2) as the sorted vector of its addresses:\n   155\t   the manifest its directory's HEAD names, when there is one, and every\n   156\t   index manifest whose load is `:loaded`.  Nothing else in the local\n   157\t   store is considered.\"\n   158\t  [node]\n   159\t  (vec (sort-by str (distinct (cond-> (vec (dht/loaded-indexes node))\n   160\t                                (head node) (conj (head node)))))))\n     1\t# DaoJing DHT: Content-Addressed Segment Distribution\n     2\t\n     3\tStatus: **contract frozen 2026-09-30 (DHT epic slice S0); S1 through S5 are\n     4\timplemented.** Section 10 records the starting tree, the slice plan, and the\n     5\tplain Clojure path S5 added. Subordinate to\n     6\t[`dao.stream.md`](./dao.stream.md), [`dao.jing.md`](./dao.jing.md) and\n     7\t[`datom.world.md`](./datom.world.md). In sections 2 to 9 every sentence is a\n     8\trule.\n     9\t\n    10\t## 1. Overview and scope\n    11\t\n    12\t`dao.jing` is deliberately dumb: it observes an explicit intake pool of\n    13\t`dao.stream` values and materializes opaque payloads into content-addressed\n    14\tstorage (see `dao.jing.md`). This document specifies the distributed\n    15\tcontent-store backend for that boundary: a Kademlia-style Distributed Hash\n    16\tTable that routes only strict content addresses.\n    17\t\n    18\tThe DHT answers one question: given a content address, where on the network\n    19\tare the bytes? It does nothing else. There are no roots, no CAS records, no\n    20\tdeletes, no source identity, no stream replication, and no consensus. Content\n    21\taddressing stays in `dao.jing` (`segment-key`); the network layer only\n    22\tdistributes the payloads those addresses name.\n    23\t\n    24\t**Strict content addresses only.** The DHT routes every registered\n    25\t`:segment/<algorithm>-<digest>` address of the closed multihash registry\n    26\t(`dao.jing.hash-registry.md`; `:blake3` default, `:sha256` selectable), and\n    27\tnothing else. The routing target is the address's digest alone; a non-segment\n    28\taddress is rejected before any local or network action. Because the payload\n    29\thashes to the address, a fetching node verifies what a peer hands it against\n    30\tthe address it asked for.\n    31\t\n    32\tNothing at this layer knows or records which stream, agent, or peer carried a\n    33\tpayload. Distribution is by content, never by provenance.\n    34\t\n    35\t**Root discovery is outside this epic (owner decision 3).** A reader holding\n    36\tonly a peer address cannot learn which manifest is current. A restart reads\n    37\tthe local HEAD of the durable-store epic; a remote query is given a manifest\n    38\taddress. Signed root facts and rendezvous are a separate later epic.\n    39\t\n    40\t## 2. Layering and composition\n    41\t\n    42\tThe governing direction, in the owner's words: \"the dht should sit on the raw\n    43\tdatagram layer but expose a dao.stream interface\"; \"Both: A raw datagram\n    44\tlayer exposed as dao.stream, AND a DHT whose own API is dao.stream-shaped,\n    45\tbuilt on it.\"\n    46\t\n    47\tThe DHT is one interpreter, `dao.jing.dht`, between two stream-shaped\n    48\tboundaries. Below it is one raw datagram socket\n    49\t([`dao.stream.datagram.md`](./dao.stream.datagram.md)). Above it is the\n    50\tcontent request medium `dao.jing.content` already defines. It is a pure\n    51\tstepped state machine: no socket, thread, atom, promise, callback, scheduler\n    52\tor clock, on any host.\n    53\t\n    54\tThe composition supplies, as data:\n    55\t\n    56\t<table>\n    57\t<tr>\n    58\t<th>\n    59\tDatum\n    60\t</th>\n    61\t<th>\n    62\tMeaning\n    63\t</th>\n721:(deftest forget-clears-a-terminal-record-and-is-refused-while-loading\n727:    (is (= ::dht/loading (refused-code #(dht/forget node a))))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
