{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/yin.vm.linker.dht.head.md | sed -n '950,1025p'; rg -n 'cookie|fragment' src/cljc/dao/stream/udp.cljc | tail -18; nl -ba src/cljc/dao/space/store/fs.cljc | sed -n '335,367p'; rg -n 'default|head-fn|table' src/cljc/yin/repl/dht.cljc | head -20\"","aggregated_output":"   950\tsource and keeps the greatest sequence; the publisher's own address in\n   951\tthe token is the mitigation. No trace says how new it is.</td></tr>\n   952\t<tr><td>A publisher that rewinds (signs an older index)</td>\n   953\t<td>The older index has a lower <code>t</code>: <code>:stale</code>. A\n   954\thigher sequence on an old index is <code>:yin.head/seq-mismatch</code>\n   955\tafter the load.</td>\n   956\t<td>A key holder can build a new index with a higher <code>t</code> that\n   957\tomits anything. The reader trusts a declared principal for its own head;\n   958\tthat is what declaring means.</td></tr>\n   959\t<tr><td>A signed trace whose sequence is wrong, replayed by anyone</td>\n   960\t<td>A candidate, loaded, refused <code>:yin.head/seq-mismatch</code>,\n   961\tdiscarded, remembered as rejected. The floor does not move; true heads\n   962\tabove the floor install as they would have. Its index is never\n   963\tresolvable.</td>\n   964\t<td>Avoid loading it once per process: the rejected set is not\n   965\tpersisted.</td></tr>\n   966\t<tr><td>Two manifests at one sequence</td>\n   967\t<td><code>:yin.head/equivocation</code>; the installed head stays.</td>\n   968\t<td>It cannot tell which the publisher meant. A greater sequence ends\n   969\tit.</td></tr>\n   970\t<tr><td>A crash while a head is being installed</td>\n   971\t<td>Before the write: the previous head, and the new one was never\n   972\tused. After the write: the new head. Never below a head that was\n   973\texposed (5.7).</td><td>-</td></tr>\n   974\t<tr><td><code>heads.edn</code> cannot be written</td>\n   975\t<td><code>:yin.head/unpersisted</code>; nothing is installed; the\n   976\tprevious head stays; the write is retried at the bounded delay.</td>\n   977\t<td>Advance while the directory refuses writes.</td></tr>\n   978\t<tr><td>Two principals, or a principal and a hand-made pin, name one\n   979\tmanifest</td>\n   980\t<td>Each holds the load; moving one releases only its own holder\n   981\t(5.5).</td><td>-</td></tr>\n   982\t<tr><td>A relay that withholds</td>\n   983\t<td>Nothing arrives from it; other sources are unaffected.</td>\n   984\t<td><strong>Withholding is undetectable</strong> when every source\n   985\twithholds: silence and \"no new head\" look the same, and no timeout may\n   986\ttell them apart here.</td></tr>\n   987\t<tr><td>A trace naming a manifest nobody holds</td>\n   988\t<td><code>:yin.head/unloadable</code>; the previous head stays; retry\n   989\tat the bounded delay; a relay never re-serves it, having not installed\n   990\tit.</td><td>-</td></tr>\n   991\t<tr><td>The publisher's directory is lost, the key kept</td>\n   992\t<td>New traces from a directory begun empty are <code>:stale</code>.\n   993\tAfter the publisher recovers with <code>--dht-recover</code> (5.8) its\n   994\ttraces continue from the old sequence.</td>\n   995\t<td>Recover on its own, short of removing the principal's record from\n   996\t<code>heads.edn</code> by hand. If the publisher cannot name its last\n   997\tmanifest, the remedy is a new key (6.5).</td></tr>\n   998\t<tr><td>The key is disclosed</td>\n   999\t<td>Whoever holds it moves the head. Remove the declaration\n  1000\t(6.5).</td><td>-</td></tr>\n  1001\t<tr><td>A source restarts</td>\n  1002\t<td><code>not-found</code> for the old ring's identity; the name is\n  1003\tresolved again and a fresh <code>:oldest</code> minted (5.3).</td>\n  1004\t<td>-</td></tr>\n  1005\t<tr><td>Spoofed askers on a serving socket</td>\n  1006\t<td>Until H5 there is no such socket off loopback: a table is refused\n  1007\ton any other bind (5.9). From H5 an unproven source draws no work and\n  1008\tno reply larger than its datagram.</td>\n  1009\t<td>Follow across machines before H5.</td></tr>\n  1010\t<tr><td>Anyone reads the board</td>\n  1011\t<td>By design. A principal's head is public where its node is reachable,\n  1012\tas its index already is under <code>--dht-publish</code>.</td>\n  1013\t<td>Restrict readers, until a gate is composed on the entry\n  1014\t(<code>dao.stream.remote.md</code> section 7).</td></tr>\n  1015\t</table>\n  1016\t\n  1017\t## 10. Implementation slices\n  1018\t\n  1019\tOrder: **H0 -> H1 -> H2 -> H3 -> H4**, with **H5** after H1 at any\n  1020\tpoint (section 12, question 5). Each lands alone with the tree green on\n  1021\tthe JVM, Node and Dart. H0 and H1 own disjoint files. H1 to H4 serve on\n  1022\tloopback only; following across machines is complete at H5.\n  1023\t\n  1024\t**H0 -- the trace and its rule.** Pure, host neutral. Files: new\n  1025\t`src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/head.cljc` (`trace`, `verify`, `seq-of`, `judge`,\n56:   whose `append!` sends toward the descriptor's address, fragmenting\n76:  \"The whole encoded datagram's budget, fragment envelope included: the\n135:(defn- fragment-envelope\n144:(defn- fragments\n148:                  (fragment-envelope id part parts direction bytes))\n206:   a single datagram when it fits the budget, fragments when it does\n210:   fragment run stops there, cleanly, nothing torn following it.\"\n225:        (loop [frags (fragments payload id direction)]\n247:(defn- fragment-envelope?\n248:  \"Any reserved fragment key present makes a datagram a fragment\n259:(defn- well-formed-fragment?\n260:  \"A fragment envelope's own wire fields, checked before any reassembly\n278:(defn- absorb-fragment!\n304:   2.1, and so is a fragment envelope whose own fields are malformed\n306:   deposits at once; a fragment envelope folds into reassembly and\n318:      (if (fragment-envelope? v)\n319:        (when (well-formed-fragment? v)\n320:          (when-some [payload (absorb-fragment! port attachment v)]\n   335\t(defn atomic-replace!\n   336\t  \"Replace `<dir>/<name>` with `text` atomically: write the whole record\n   337\t   to a temp file beside it, sync the temp, rename it over the target,\n   338\t   and sync the directory where the host supports it — a failed\n   339\t   directory sync fails the replacement. A reader observes either the\n   340\t   whole previous record or the whole new one, never a partial write.\n   341\t\n   342\t   `before-rename`, `(fn [temp-path])`, runs in the one window a crash\n   343\t   can interrupt — after the temp is synced, before the rename — so a\n   344\t   test can interrupt the replacement there; a throw leaves the target\n   345\t   exactly as it was.\"\n   346\t  ([dir name text] (atomic-replace! dir name text {}))\n   347\t  ([dir name text {:keys [before-rename]}]\n   348\t   (let [target (str dir \"/\" name)\n   349\t         temp (str dir \"/\" name \".tmp-\" (random-uuid))]\n   350\t     #?(:cljd (try (.writeAsStringSync (dart-io/File. temp) text .flush true)\n   351\t                   (when before-rename (before-rename temp))\n   352\t                   (.renameSync (dart-io/File. temp) target)\n   353\t                   (catch Object e\n   354\t                     (throw (ex-info (str \"cannot replace \" target \": \" e)\n   355\t                                     {:dir dir :target target}\n   356\t                                     e))))\n   357\t        :clj (try (with-open [out (java.io.FileOutputStream. ^String temp)]\n   358\t                    (.write out (.getBytes ^String text \"UTF-8\"))\n   359\t                    (.flush out)\n   360\t                    (.sync (.getFD out)))\n   361\t                  (when before-rename (before-rename temp))\n   362\t                  (java.nio.file.Files/move\n   363\t                    (java.nio.file.Paths/get temp (make-array String 0))\n   364\t                    (java.nio.file.Paths/get target (make-array String 0))\n   365\t                    (into-array java.nio.file.StandardCopyOption\n   366\t                                [java.nio.file.StandardCopyOption/ATOMIC_MOVE\n   367\t                                 java.nio.file.StandardCopyOption/REPLACE_EXISTING]))\n41:(def default-max-inbound-bytes\n42:  \"The CLI default of the inbound storage bound; `dao.space.dht`'s.\"\n43:  dht/default-max-inbound-bytes)\n77:                            :bind! (or bind! (dht/default-bind))})\n84:               :head-fn (fn [manifest-address]\n85:                          ((:head-fn base) manifest-address)\n90:      (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e\n208:    ((:head-fn (dht/local node)) manifest)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
