 request-get / request-materialize / step / abandon\n246:(defn request-get\n   306\t   deposits at once; a fragment envelope folds into reassembly and\n   307\t   deposits only once complete -- loss of any part is loss of the\n   308\t   whole message, recovered by the link's resend rule, not by this\n   309\t   port. Replies to what this call learns go to `host`:`src-port`,\n   310\t   this datagram's own source, never an address a payload might\n   311\t   claim.\"\n   312\t  [port host src-port bytes]\n   313\t  (when-some [v (try (cbor/decode bytes) (catch #?(:cljd Object\n   314\t                                                   :clj Throwable\n   315\t                                                   :cljs :default) _\n   316\t                                           nil))]\n   317\t    (let [attachment (address-key host src-port)]\n   318\t      (if (fragment-envelope? v)\n   319\t        (when (well-formed-fragment? v)\n   320\t          (when-some [payload (absorb-fragment! port attachment v)]\n   321\t            (when-some [whole (try (cbor/decode payload)\n   322\t                                   (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable\n   323\t                                             :cljs :default) _\n   324\t                                     nil))]\n   325\t              (deposit! port attachment host src-port whole))))\n   326\t        (deposit! port attachment host src-port v)))))\n   327\t\n   328\t\n   329\t;; =============================================================================\n   330\t;; The projection: one channel ring per attachment (this channel's\n   331\t;; ws-project)\n   332\t;; =============================================================================\n   333\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"agent_message","text":"The revision gives concrete rules and tests for the original eight findings. Two gaps remain in the load lifecycle: it does not explain how a newer head bypasses an unfinished candidate load, or how retrying a failed shared load works. H1 also changes `forget` in a way that contradicts an existing test it requires to pass unchanged. I’ll check whether H5’s cookie gate covers fragments before finalizing the review."}}
